diagnosis_text:
I could not reproduce any reachability problem to the partner network. The routing/control-plane subsystem (FRR BGP) and the data-plane on all links are healthy. End-to-end tests show pc1 (195.11.14.2) can reach pc2 (200.1.1.2) with 0% loss and normal RTTs. On router1 and router2, BGP is established over eth0 (193.10.11.1 <-> 193.10.11.2) and each side is exchanging one IPv4 unicast prefix: router1 advertises 195.11.14.0/24 and learns 200.1.1.0/24; router2 advertises 200.1.1.0/24 and learns 195.11.14.0/24. Both prefixes are installed in the RIB/FIB (B>* entries present) and host defaults point to their local routers.

Mechanism: With BGP up and correct network statements, traffic between the two LANs forwards via router1 eth0 to router2 eth0 as expected; no filters or policy are blocking eBGP (“no bgp ebgp-requires-policy” is configured), so advertisements and forwarding are intact.

Localization: FRR bgpd on router1/router2 and interfaces eth0/eth1 are operational; no interface errors or missing routes observed.

Root cause: No network fault was found; the reported outage is not reproducible in this lab and was likely transient or external (e.g., DNS/application-side issue).

Corrective fix: No changes required on the network. Recommend the user re-test their application/service and verify DNS/port reachability to the partner. Continue monitoring BGP sessions and logs for flaps, but current connectivity between 195.11.14.0/24 and 200.1.1.0/24 is normal. 
